# Phase E (#47, flip brick B3) — the stage-0 SEED anchor.
#
# Most of krapped/ is machine-generated and ignored, BUT the deterministic TEXT output of
# a one-time libclang generation is COMMITTED as the bootstrap seed: post-B5 (libclang
# reducer deleted from in-tree krapper_gen) this module can no longer (re)parse its own
# Clang-slice headers, so it builds from this committed seed under
# -Pkpp.frontend.clangwalk=seed (now its default — see root gradle.properties).
#
# Committed (deterministic, portable): the Kotlin bindings (src/), the C++ wrapper
# (clangwalk.cc / clangwalk.h) and the forcing headers (KrapperForce_*.h, includes
# hand-relativized to ../include/clang_slice.h — the #86 absolute-path generator bug).
# Everything else — the compiled wrapper object (libclangwalk.a, host/LLVM-pinned), the
# cinterop .def (carries this checkout's absolute krapped path), generated.txt, fixups.json,
# cpp-models/, *.log — stays machine-generated/ignored and is regenerated at build (the .def
# + .a by runSeedSync, a plain C++ compile with no libclang parse).
/krapped/*
!/krapped/requested.txt
!/krapped/src
!/krapped/src/**
!/krapped/*.cc
!/krapped/*.h
